{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And I will give.</b> This too was a wondrous thing, that the Egyptians were appeasing Israel to ask of them. This is the sense of וישאילום (and they let them ask), and this is contrary to the way of the people of the world." "Know that the mem of ריקם is superfluous, and the word is found both for the plural and also in feminine language: אל תבואי ריקם (do not come empty) (Ruth 3:17), and like it חנם (Genesis 29:15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:25.718605174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}